# -*- text -*-
######################################################################
#
#  ECLOUD: per-NAS listeners for Cisco Meraki cloud-sourced RADIUS
#  (multi-vendor Cycle E, D-044; SECURITY_ARCHITECTURE.md §3.5).
#
#  Every rendered file in meraki.d/ holds, per Meraki NAS:
#    clients meraki_<id> { client ... { ipaddr = <Meraki source CIDR>
#                                       secret = <that NAS's secret>
#                                       shortname = <nas_clients.id> } }
#    listen { type = auth, port = <auth>,     clients = meraki_<id>, virtual_server = ecloud }
#    listen { type = acct, port = <auth + 1>, clients = meraki_<id>, virtual_server = ecloud }
#  so a packet is authenticated with a PER-NAS secret although every Meraki
#  customer shares the same source addresses. The `ecloud` server passes
#  %{client:shortname} to the API, which resolves a Meraki NAS by it ONLY and
#  also requires the registered NAS-Identifier.
#
#  Default (MERAKI_CLOUD_RADIUS_ENABLED=false): meraki.d/ holds only comments
#  and nothing listens. FreeRADIUS reads listeners at start-up only, so a
#  re-rendered file needs a container restart (same as clients.d/).
#
######################################################################

$INCLUDE ${confdir}/meraki.d/
